<Base title="About — Dylan Norquist" description="About Dylan Norquist: CS student at MSOE, Applied AI Intern at Direct Supply, machine learning and low-level programming.">
  <main class="page-container">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I'm Dylan Norquist, a developer who likes building projects in his free
        time. I'm an Applied AI Intern at Direct Supply, where I previously
        worked as a Data Science and Software Engineering Intern. I build rapid
        prototypes in Python, PostgreSQL, and React — full-stack applications
        that apply AI to problems in the elderly care industry.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm a Computer Science major at the Milwaukee School of Engineering
        (MSOE) with a focus in Machine Learning and Low Level Programming. My
        undergraduate research has been on Behavior Cloning from online videos,
        and Fall 2025 I'll be researching Reinforcement Learning for
        generalization and world modeling.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of school and work I rock climb, play video games, and code.
        My favorite project so far is a working neural network running on an
        8-bit computer inside Minecraft. A close second is sending a V9 boulder
        problem by dynoing to the top and skipping the entire problem.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site exists mostly so I have somewhere to write things down. I
        plan to keep tinkering with it as I go.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
